Subject: [ZEROX 3/4] Budget primed TNT explosions per world tick

Files modified by the generated source patch:

- net/minecraft/world/entity/item/PrimedTnt.java
- io/papermc/paper/zerox/ZeroxExplosionLimiter.java

Core behavior:

```diff
 if (fuse <= 0) {
+    if (level instanceof ServerLevel serverLevel
+        && !ZeroxExplosionLimiter.tryAcquire(serverLevel)) {
+        this.setFuse(1);
+        return;
+    }
     explode();
 }
```

The limiter maintains a weak per-world budget keyed by the current game tick. An explosion proceeds only while both limits remain available:

- maximum explosions per tick;
- maximum elapsed explosion-scheduling time for that tick.

Strict defaults:

```properties
tnt.max-explosions-per-tick=4
tnt.max-processing-ms-per-tick=3
```

Properties are read from `.zerox/zerox.properties` and exposed as JVM system properties before server initialization.

Safety properties:

- The TNT entity remains alive with a one-tick fuse when deferred.
- Explosion events and world mutation remain on the authoritative server thread.
- No Bukkit event is called asynchronously.
- Event ordering within the explosions processed during a tick remains synchronous.

Tradeoff:

Huge chain reactions take more ticks to complete. This is deliberate load shedding; it protects server responsiveness rather than pretending tens of thousands of explosions can finish instantly at 20 TPS.
